ly. Semin Fetal Neonatal Med. 2005;10:73–81. doi: 10.1016/j.siny.2004.09.005. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 53. Simon E, Janette R, Des B, et al. Sildenafil (Viagra) in childhood and neonatal pulmonary hypertension. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2002;39(Suppl 2):402. [ Google Scholar ] 54. Namachivayam P, Theilen U, Butt WW, et al. Sildenafil prevents rebound pulmonary hypertension after withdrawal of nitric oxide in children. Am J Respir Crit Care Med. 2006;174:1042–1047. doi: 10.1164/rccm.200605-694OC. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 55. Raja SG, Danton MD, MacArthur KJ, et al. Effects of escalating doses of sildenafil on hemodynamics and gas exchange in children with pulmonary hypertension and congenital cardiac defects. J Cardiothorac Vasc Anesth. 2007;21:203–207. doi: 10.1053/j.jvca.2006.02.010. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 56. Ajami GH, Borzoee M, Radvar M, et al. Comparison of the effectiveness of oral sildenafil versus oxygen administration as a test for feasibility of operation for patients with secondary pulmonary arterial hypertension. Pediatr Cardiol. 2008;29:552–555. doi: 10.1007/s00246-007-9139-2. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 57. Lee JE, Hillier SC, Knoderer CA. Use of sildenafil to facilitate weaning from inhaled nitric oxide in children with pulmonary hypertension following surgery for congenital heart disease. J Intensive Care Med. 2008;23:329–334. doi: 10.1177/0885066608321389. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 58. Hunter L, Richens T, Davis C, et al. Sildenafil use in congenital diaphragmatic hernia. Arch Dis Child Fetal Neonatal Ed. 2009;94:F467. doi: 10.1136/adc.2008.153684. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 59. Uhm JY, Jhang WK, Park JJ, et al. Postoperative use of oral sildenafil in pediatric patients with congenital heart disease. Pediatr Cardiol. 2010;31:515–520. doi: 10.1007/s00246-009-9632-x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 60. Nemoto S, Sasaki T, Ozawa H, et al. Oral sildenafil for persistent pulmonary h