INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(1345,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1418214','Developmental paediatrics in primary care: what should we teach?','Baird G, Hall DM.','1985','badly embark whitmore entrant cradle bicknell tb01544 chaplais walkers a070810 blakemore anisometropic frankenburg natta demersseman frankenburg fandal sciarillo frankenburg doorninck liddell prescreening tb15245 spavins neligan prudham tb01460 uninitiated tb13847 skuse tb00172 tb15154','Abstract There is little agreement about what constitutes good developmental paediatric practice at the level of primary care. Many of the available screening tests are intrinsically unsatisfactory or badly performed, but screening is only a small part of developmental paediatrics. Every primary care doctor should be familiar with the scientific basis of the subject even if a decision is made not to embark on a formal screening programme. Full text PDF Previous 583 584 585 586 Next Selected References These references are in PubMed. This may not be the complete list of references from this article. Bax M., Whitmore K. Neurodevelopmental screening in the school-entrant medical examination. Lancet. 1973 Aug 18;2(7825):368–370. doi: 10.1016/s0140-6736(73)93205-4. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Bhattacharya J., Bennett M. J., Tucker S. M. Long term follow up of newborns tested with the auditory response cradle. Arch Dis Child. 1984 Jun;59(6):504–511. doi: 10.1136/adc.59.6.504. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Bicknell J. The psychopathology of handicap. Br J Med Psychol. 1983 Jun;56(Pt 2):167–178. doi: 10.1111/j.2044-8341.1983.tb01544.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Chaplais J. D., Macfarlane J. A. A review of 404 ''late walkers''. Arch Dis Child. 1984 Jun;59(6):512–516. doi: 10.1136/adc.59.6.512. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Cochrane A. L., Holland W. W. Validation of screening procedures. Br Med Bull. 1971 Jan;27(1):3–8. doi: 10.1093/oxford