INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(1394,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC473257','Micro methods and micro apparatus for chemical pathology with special reference to paediatrics.','Clayton BE, Jenkins P.','1966','conveniently technicon drekter technic saponification microelectrophoresis huggett dianisidine natelson ultramicro nonprotein fingertip ultramicro pipets microgasometer ibbott pinfield ultramicro iggo scandrett bj0580426 reinouts haga wael ultramicro s0065 saifer gerstenfeld zymaris microchemical ultramicro seligson microchemistry gerarde semiautomatic microspecimens','Abstract This article describes methods and apparatus which permit the estimation of a particular substance without requiring more blood than can conveniently and safely be removed from a child by capillary puncture. No reference will be made to the use of methods on the Technicon Auto-Analyzer as that machine is not yet generally geared to paediatric work, although a few centres have made their own modifications to permit certain methods to be performed on capillary samples of blood. Full text PDF Previous 293 294 295 296 297 Next Selected References These references are in PubMed. This may not be the complete list of references from this article. CARR J. J., DREKTER I. J. Simplified rapid technic for the extraction and determination of serum cholesterol without saponification. Clin Chem. 1956 Oct;2(5):353–368. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] FLYNN F. V., DE MAYO P. Microelectrophoresis of protein on filter-paper. Lancet. 1951 Aug 11;2(6676):235–239. doi: 10.1016/s0140-6736(51)93239-4. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] HUGGETT A. S., NIXON D. A. Use of glucose oxidase, peroxidase, and O-dianisidine in determination of blood and urinary glucose. Lancet. 1957 Aug 24;273(6991):368–370. doi: 10.1016/s0140-6736(57)92595-3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] KING J. Routine methods for the estimation of serum transaminase. J Med Lab Technol. 1958 Jan;15(1):17–22. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 